    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d469">

                <pb facs="0485" n="1219" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1219"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Dupuy de Lôme to Mr. Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Spain at Washington</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-01-03"><hi rendition="#italic">January 3,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary</hi>: Referring to my note of the 31st
                    ultimo, and in reply to yours of yesterday, I have the honor to confirm all that
                    I said with respect to the request of the firm of E. Atkins &amp; Co., and I
                    take pleasure in informing you that these gentlemen have repeatedly expressed to
                    me their satisfaction with the zeal and energy with which the Spanish
                    authorities of the Island of Cuba endeavor to protect their property and
                    interests from the attacks of the insurgents.</p>
                <p>I avail, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">E. Dupuy de Lôme.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
